module examples.err_dma_shared_lend_wrapped

# plans/M7.md item I (the adversarial sweep), 03-hardware.md §3,
# `DmaShared[P, L]`'s own second sentence: "It cannot be read as bytes or
# **lent as a plain value**."
#
# `golden/err-dma-shared-lend` rejects the direct spelling
# (`read ring: DmaShared[BlockControl, RingControl]`). One plain wrapper
# struct away it was accepted: `dma_shared_in_type` walked the type
# structurally — arrays, tuples, `Option`, `Result`, `fn`, and a named
# type's *type arguments* — but never into a named type's declared
# **fields**, unlike `type_contains_capability`, which has had exactly
# that reach since item A built it for "at any nesting". So `read bundle:
# RingBundle` handed out the same ordinary borrow of a descriptor ring,
# carrying none of the target's volatile/cache/ordering semantics, which
# is the whole class of bug 03 §3's sealed queue operations exist to make
# unwritable.
#
# WHY IT SURVIVED THIS LONG, which is the interesting part: `DmaShared`
# *is* one of the five capability types (`CAPABILITY_TYPES`), so the
# containment rules — which do walk fields — already caught the wrapper
# everywhere they apply: an `@actor` field, an `@actor` parameter, a `pub`
# method of either kind, a fn return. The one place left is a `@driver`'s
# own **private** method, which containment deliberately permits (a driver
# may hold capabilities; that asymmetry is §1's rule). That is exactly
# where this file puts it, and it is exactly where a real driver would
# write one.
#
# The diagnostic names the parameter's own declared type *and* what it
# carries: `RingBundle` alone would not say why it is refused, and
# `DmaShared[...]` alone would not match anything the author wrote.
#
# `take` is untouched — `golden/check-dma-shared` is the accept, and
# moving the handle is how it reaches a driver at all.

@layout(dma, endian=little)
struct RingControl:
    flags: u16
    idx: u16

struct BlockHw:
    id: u32

pool BlockControl

struct RingBundle:
    ring: DmaShared[BlockControl, RingControl]

@driver
pub struct BlkDriver:
    sectors: u64

    fn peek_ring(read self, read bundle: RingBundle) -> unit:
        return unit
